WHY THERE IS NO LICENSE YET

These documents describe Microware OS-9, which is not a historical curiosity:
it remains a commercial product, still sold and still ported to new
processors, with an active rights holder.

The material here was assembled from publicly published documentation and
from original testing against emulators, and was written specifically to
avoid reproducing Microware's proprietary text or code — the prose is
original, no worked code examples are preserved verbatim, and no file mirrors
a source's structure. README.md and each skill's SOURCES.md set out that
chain in detail, including the material that was deliberately left unread.

Care taken in good faith is still not the same as terms agreed. What may
properly be published, and under what license, is Microware's to weigh in on
first. This notice stands until they have had that opportunity.

A license file will replace this notice after review by Microware.


IF YOU HAVE BEEN GIVEN A COPY

Read it, use it, and say what you think of it. Please do not redistribute it
or post it publicly. If anything here misstates OS-9, or reads to you as
going further than it should with Microware's material, say so — that is
what this review period is for.
